  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The six-membered cyclic structure of glucose is called pyranose structure (&alpha;&ndash; or &beta;&ndash;), in analogy with pyran. Pyran is a cyclic organic compound with one oxygen atom and five carbon atoms in the ring.&nbsp;The cyclic structure of glucose is more correctly represented by Haworth structure</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0055_2fd13a510f89.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 232px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi></math>&nbsp;are cis.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are anti to each other.</p><p>So,the correct option is B.</p>"
  }
